#
# D-0280: one authentication in the installation, and it is NOESAR's.
#
# Owner instruction, verbatim: "no devi eliminarli password e token devi usare quelli di
# noesar e un modulo ora". D-0279 built the bearer-token path but left the credential to be
# minted by hand, with the Owner typing a password into a tool — the same friction D-0277
# already rejected for module installation. So NOESAR issues it, to itself, at boot.
#
# `ensureModuleServiceAccounts()` runs after tool seeding: load-or-create, deliberately the
# same idiom as `loadOrCreateOwnerSigningKey()`, because a service token is readable exactly
# once at issue and the FILE therefore has to be the source of truth. Every later boot
# re-verifies the stored token still authenticates and reissues only if it does not, so an
# operator revoking it is honoured rather than papered over. The credential is written to
# `${workspace}/module-credentials/<module>.token` at mode 0600 and never leaves this side
# over the network and never becomes an environment variable here.
#
# Consuming module (Debug Evolution, a separate product) mounts that one directory
# read-only and reads the file per request, so a reissue takes effect on the next call
# rather than at its next restart.
#
# Verified before this build: unit 1407/1408 (1 pre-existing skip, 0 failed), ESLint 276
# files 0 errors. Built FROM the previous tag: layers well under the 128 limit.

FROM noesar-evolution:phase4-service-token-auth

LABEL org.noesar.phase="4-module-credentials"
LABEL org.noesar.feature="noesar-provisions-its-official-modules-own-credential-at-boot"
LABEL org.noesar.base-image="noesar-evolution:phase4-service-token-auth"

USER root
COPY --chown=10001:10001 services/reference-control-plane/ /opt/noesar/services/reference-control-plane/
USER 10001:10001
